It appears there's a misunderstanding in the request, similar to the previous 'B150' query. The 'B170' designation was used for the first generation Mercedes-Benz B-Class (W245), produced roughly between 2005 and 2011.

There is no "most recent version" of a B170, as the current B-Class generation (W247, launched 2019) uses designations like B180, B200, B220, B250, B200d, etc.

Since I cannot evaluate a non-existent "most recent B170" and must adhere strictly to the provided data without guessing or extrapolating, I will return default `0.00` values for all metrics, reflecting the ambiguity of the request.

